icians need to know now also if you  look at it from the patient side  advanced cancer patients need help by  definition  these are patients that have exhausted  standard of care  they have less than one in two chance of  a five year survival  so by default they are often very very  scared and confused  um there's also an urgent sense of  finding  innovative therapies to help themselves  and because of the state that they're at  they're also  trying to google online look online for  um  for more information about treatments  they should consider so they also need  help in  understanding these options as well  so what we're proposing is uh what if we  can actually develop a patient-centric  position oncology platform  that's sort of what we've done here at x  cures where  you want to empower patients and their  doctors uh  with the right information so that they  could prioritize and access the best  treatment options and test  to help them beat advanced cancer  utilizing  artificial intelligence and machine  learning tools integrating public data  for information such as  clinicalchild.gov for party  proprietary knowledge from physicians in  terms of what they have done in the past  and why  and expert in sites as well so what we  want to do is create a learning system  that's efficiently incorporating results  from all patients  on all therapies at all times  if you also think about it from sort of  drug development  company standpoint as well as i'm sure  many of you  are aware the vast majority of patients  over 95 percent of patients  don't qualify or don't participate in  clinical trials  it's maybe because of um it's not near  where they currently live they're not  able to travel  to those sites or they don't meet the  inclusion exclusion criteria  and to give you a sense of the overall  market here as well  advanced cancer kills over 600 000  patients annually in the united states  so what if you can also learn and also  give  access to the 95 percent of patients  that can't  get into clinical trials what if you can  get them access to these  investigational therapies through right  to try  or manage access programs for example  and  you can still continuously learn from  them by gathering the real world data  through prospective observational  studies  and so this gives you the ability to  learn from all patients and you can then  also then give that learning back to in  order to help future patients as well  so in order to build this platform these  are the the challenges that  we have defined and have solved in order  to  build this platform to help patients so  first of all you  need to be able to understand the  patient that you're trying to help  right um you need to understand what we  call the cancer journey what is their  current  clinical situation you also need to be  able to track  longitudinal outcomes as well in order  to do that  on the bottom left side you can see our  solution  you really need to be able to build a  means to  gather real world data in a hipaa  compliant storage  a master protocol for a good clinical  practice or gcp  and also data that structured  structuring the data  in the right way so that it could be  regulatory grade and could be used for  future submissions for example  by pharma to the fda  you also then need to know the right  treatments what should be considered for  these patients  and also how to get it as well because  it's not useful to present  patients and physicians with options  that  they don't know how to get access to for  these treatments  so what you need to do is build an  options library  with a list of treatment options but  also present  why what we call the medical rationales  why  physicians historically has recommended  such um  treatment options to patients and also  how do you access these  therapies that they may be interested in  and finally you also need an engine  that can recommend the right options and  you also want to learn  from it as well so a l